To build the backend workflow for the Manual Entry, we need to implement the core state machine. This involves three distinct phases: **Initialization** (when the Maker submits the manual grid), **Routing** (fetching the correct batches for the logged-in Checker), and **Progression** (the Checkers approving/rejecting the batch).
Here is the exact step-by-step implementation guide to wire this up in your Spring Boot backend.
### Step 1: Initialize the Workflow (The Maker Submission)
When the user submits the Manual Entry grid from the frontend, it hits your createBatchRequest method. We need to update this method to register the batch in the new VOUCHER_POSTING table and set its initial state.
**File to Update:** VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java (or your equivalent service class)
Find your createBatchRequest method and add the workflow initialization logic right after you save the initial batch details.
**ADD THIS CODE BLOCK:**
```java
    // ... inside createBatchRequest, after saving to JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER ...

    // 1. Map the Creator's Role ID to the Role Name (Adjust IDs based on your DB)
    String roleName = (creatorRole == 51) ? "TCSGLIF" : (creatorRole == 52 ? "SBIGLIF" : "OTHER");

    // 2. Initialize the Multi-Level Workflow State
    VoucherPosting posting = new VoucherPosting();
    posting.setBatchId(batchId);
    posting.setVidFk(dto.getVid()); // Received from your new frontend payload
    posting.setCreatorsRole(roleName);
    posting.setCreatedBy(creatorId);
    posting.setCurrentStatus("PENDING_L1"); 
    
    // 3. Determine the specific Approval Route
    if ("TCSGLIF".equalsIgnoreCase(roleName)) {
        posting.setApprovalWorkflow("W1_3_APPROVERS"); // Route 1: TCS -> SBI -> SBI
        posting.setNextApproval("TCSGLIF"); 
    } else {
        posting.setApprovalWorkflow("W2_4_APPROVERS"); // Route 2: TCS -> TCS -> SBI -> SBI
        posting.setNextApproval("TCSGLIF"); 
    }

    // 4. Handle the Optional Scheduling from the frontend
    if (dto.getScheduledTime() != null && !dto.getScheduledTime().isEmpty()) {
        posting.setExecutionScheduled("YES");
        posting.setScheduledTime(LocalDateTime.parse(dto.getScheduledTime().replace(" ", "T")));
        posting.setIsScheduleOverride("NO");
    } else {
        posting.setExecutionScheduled("NO");
    }
    
    // Save to the database
    voucherPostingRepository.save(posting);

```
### Step 2: The Checker Dashboard API (Role-Based Routing)
When a Checker logs in, they should *only* see batches that are currently waiting for their specific role's approval. We need to create a fetch method that joins JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER with our VOUCHER_POSTING table.
**File to Update:** VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java
**ADD THIS METHOD:**
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getPendingBatchesForChecker(Integer userRole) {
        // Map the logged-in user's role
        String roleName = (userRole == 51) ? "TCSGLIF" : (userRole == 52 ? "SBIGLIF" : "OTHER");

        // Fetch only batches where NEXT_APPROVAL matches the current user's role
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                b.BATCH_ID, p.VID_FK, b.CREATOR_ID, b.REQ_DATE, b.BATCH_REMARKS, 
                b.TOTAL_ROWS, b.TOTAL_DEBIT, b.TOTAL_CREDIT, 
                p.CURRENT_STATUS, p.NEXT_APPROVAL, p.SCHEDULED_TIME
            FROM JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER b
            INNER JOIN VOUCHER_POSTING p ON b.BATCH_ID = p.BATCH_ID
            WHERE p.NEXT_APPROVAL = ? 
              AND p.CURRENT_STATUS LIKE 'PENDING_%'
            ORDER BY b.REQ_DATE DESC
        """;

        return jdbcTemplate.query(sql, (rs, rowNum) -> {
            Map<String, Object> map = new HashMap<>();
            map.put("batchId", rs.getString("BATCH_ID"));
            map.put("vid", rs.getString("VID_FK"));
            map.put("creatorId", rs.getString("CREATOR_ID"));
            map.put("requestDate", rs.getTimestamp("REQ_DATE"));
            map.put("remarks", rs.getString("BATCH_REMARKS"));
            map.put("totalRows", rs.getLong("TOTAL_ROWS"));
            map.put("totalAmount", rs.getBigDecimal("TOTAL_DEBIT"));
            map.put("workflowState", rs.getString("CURRENT_STATUS"));
            
            Timestamp scheduled = rs.getTimestamp("SCHEDULED_TIME");
            map.put("scheduledTime", scheduled != null ? scheduled.toLocalDateTime().toString() : null);

            return map;
        }, roleName); 
    }

```
### Step 3: The State Machine Engine (Approval/Rejection)
This is the most critical part of the backend. It enforces the business rules (no self-approval, no duplicate approvals) and moves the state from L1 to L2 to L3.
**File to Update:** VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java
**ADD THIS METHOD:**
```java
    @Transactional
    public void processWorkflowAction(ProcessVoucherRequestDto dto, String executorId, Integer executorRole) {
        String batchId = dto.getBatchId();
        
        VoucherPosting posting = voucherPostingRepository.findById(batchId)
                .orElseThrow(() -> new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Batch ID not found."));

        // 1. Business Rule: Prevent Self-Approval
        if (executorId.equalsIgnoreCase(posting.getCreatedBy())) {
            throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Security Violation: You cannot approve a batch you created.");
        }

        // 2. Business Rule: Prevent Duplicate Approvals
        boolean hasAlreadyApproved = voucherWorkflowRepository.findByBatchIdFkOrderByLastActionAtAsc(batchId)
                .stream().anyMatch(w -> executorId.equalsIgnoreCase(w.getLastActionBy()));
        if (hasAlreadyApproved) {
            throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Security Violation: You have already approved this batch at a previous level.");
        }

        // 3. Process Rejection
        if (dto.getStatus() == RequestStatus.REJECTED) {
            posting.setCurrentStatus("REJECTED");
            posting.setNextApproval(null);
            voucherPostingRepository.save(posting);
            
            logWorkflowAction(batchId, posting.getVidFk(), "REJECTED", executorId, dto.getRemarks());
            
            jdbcTemplate.update("UPDATE JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER SET BATCH_STATUS = 'REJECTED' WHERE BATCH_ID = ?", batchId);
            return;
        }

        // 4. State Machine Progression (Approval)
        boolean isFinalApproval = false;
        String nextState = "";
        String nextRoleRequired = "";

        if ("W1_3_APPROVERS".equals(posting.getApprovalWorkflow())) {
            switch (posting.getCurrentStatus()) {
                case "PENDING_L1": nextState = "PENDING_L2"; nextRoleRequired = "SBIGLIF"; break; 
                case "PENDING_L2": nextState = "PENDING_L3"; nextRoleRequired = "SBIGLIF"; break; 
                case "PENDING_L3": isFinalApproval = true; break; 
            }
        } else if ("W2_4_APPROVERS".equals(posting.getApprovalWorkflow())) {
            switch (posting.getCurrentStatus()) {
                case "PENDING_L1": nextState = "PENDING_L2"; nextRoleRequired = "TCSGLIF"; break; 
                case "PENDING_L2": nextState = "PENDING_L3"; nextRoleRequired = "SBIGLIF"; break; 
                case "PENDING_L3": nextState = "PENDING_L4"; nextRoleRequired = "SBIGLIF"; break; 
                case "PENDING_L4": isFinalApproval = true; break; 
            }
        }

        if (isFinalApproval) {
            // Check Schedule Logic
            if ("YES".equalsIgnoreCase(posting.getExecutionScheduled()) && posting.getScheduledTime().isAfter(LocalDateTime.now())) {
                posting.setCurrentStatus("SCHEDULED");
                logWorkflowAction(batchId, posting.getVidFk(), "FINAL_APPROVED_SCHEDULED", executorId, dto.getRemarks());
            } else {
                posting.setCurrentStatus("POSTED");
                posting.setExecutedAt(LocalDateTime.now());
                logWorkflowAction(batchId, posting.getVidFk(), "FINAL_APPROVED_POSTED", executorId, dto.getRemarks());
                
                // TRIGGER YOUR ORACLE DB PROCEDURE HERE (e.g., PROCESS_JOURNAL_BATCH)
                executeOraclePostingProcedure(batchId, executorId, dto.getRemarks());
            }
            posting.setNextApproval(null);
        } else {
            posting.setCurrentStatus(nextState);
            posting.setNextApproval(nextRoleRequired);
            logWorkflowAction(batchId, posting.getVidFk(), "APPROVED_" + posting.getCurrentStatus(), executorId, dto.getRemarks());
        }

        voucherPostingRepository.save(posting);
    }

    private void logWorkflowAction(String batchId, String vid, String action, String executorId, String remarks) {
        VoucherWorkflow wf = new VoucherWorkflow();
        wf.setBatchIdFk(batchId);
        wf.setVidFk(vid);
        wf.setLastAction(action);
        wf.setLastActionBy(executorId);
        wf.setRemarks(remarks);
        voucherWorkflowRepository.save(wf);
    }

```
